> array subscript 0 is outside array bounds of 'char[]' [-Werror=array-bounds]

Yea, that is because `Warray-bounds` does some static analysis on the pointer/array index dereferences.

Note that [`chunk_p` is assigned `ptr_to_chunk(allocated)` in L746](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/picolibc/blob/e87b2fc37345a62361478f0a6efd140e14180ba5/newlib/libc/stdlib/nano-mallocr.c#L746), where `allocated` is a memory block allocated by `malloc`:

```c
chunk_p = ptr_to_chunk(allocated);
```

This resolves to `(chunk_t *)((char *)allocated - MALLOC_HEAD)`, which is below index 0 in terms of the "array index":

```c
static inline chunk_t *
ptr_to_chunk(void * ptr)
{
    return (chunk_t *) ((char *) ptr - MALLOC_HEAD);
}
```

So [dereferencing it in L761](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/picolibc/blob/e87b2fc37345a62361478f0a6efd140e14180ba5/newlib/libc/stdlib/nano-mallocr.c#L761) is flagged by the static analysis:

```c
new_chunk_p->size = chunk_p->size - offset;
```

@keith-packard since this code explicitly does an "unsafe access," disabling `Warray-bounds` (for this entire file or only the affected lines) would make sense. The "static analysis" feature was added in GCC 11 (see https://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc/commit/6450f07388f9fe575a489c9309c36012b17b88b0).

> Which compiler version is generating this warning?

@keith-packard https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/46967#issuecomment-1172204414

It was in GCC 12.1, but the same warning should be displayed in GCC 11.x as well.
